  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "FlashLoan & price manipulation. Lost: $6k"
    },
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "Incorrect price calculation via getReverse APC price relies on the reserve balances of the corresponding PancakeSwap pair. You dump APC token price by flashloan. Vulnerable code snippet: Attack tx: https://explorer.phalcon.xyz/tx/bsc/0xbcaecea2044101c80f186ce5327bec796cd9e054f0c240ddce93e2aead337370 https://explorer.phalcon.xyz/tx/bsc/0xf2d4559aeb945fb8e4304da5320ce6a2a96415aa70286715c9fcaf5dbd9d7ed2 Analysis: https://twitter.com/BlockSecTeam/status/1598262002010378241"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "The APC (ArenaPlay) swap contract on BNB Chain was exploited on 1 December 2022 via flash-loan-driven spot price manipulation, allowing attackers to drain approximately $6,000 in project token reserves by abusing a vulnerable on-chain price oracle. The swap contract priced internal APC–MUSD conversions using the live spot price from a PancakeSwap AMM pool. Attackers manipulated the spot price with flash loans, allowing them to swap at artificially inflated/deflated rates in the same transaction without resistance."
    }
  ],
